Search jobs here{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"JobPosting","title":"Growth Lead / GTM Lead (India)","description":"<p>We are looking for an ambitious and strategic <strong>Growth Lead / GTM Lead</strong> to drive <strong>the company's</strong> market entry and expansion across the <strong>United States, United Kingdom, and Germany</strong>. This is a senior, high-ownership role at the intersection of business development, marketing strategy, and sales execution. You will build <strong>the company's</strong> pipeline from the ground up in these markets, establish key partnerships, and own the full go-to-market motion from brand positioning to deal closure.</p> <p>This role is ideal for someone who has sold B2B professional services, consulting, or technology solutions to mid-market and enterprise buyers in Western markets and understands the nuances of building trust-led relationships across geographies.</p> <p><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p> <p><strong>Go-to-Market Strategy</strong></p> <ul> <li>Develop and execute GTM strategies tailored for the US, UK, and Germany markets, accounting for regional buyer behaviour, competitive landscape, and cultural nuances.</li> <li>Define Ideal Customer Profiles (ICPs), value propositions, and messaging frameworks for each market.</li> <li>Identify the most effective channels outbound, partnerships, events, and digital and build a scalable playbook.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Pipeline & Revenue Generation</strong></p> <ul> <li>Own and drive outbound prospecting by identifying target companies (mid-market to enterprise) and decision-makers (C-suite, VP Engineering, VP Operations, CFOs), considering offshoring or setting up GCCs.</li> <li>Build and manage a healthy, qualified pipeline across all three markets using CRM tools.</li> <li>Lead discovery calls, capability presentations, and proposal conversations through to closure.</li> <li>Meet or exceed quarterly revenue and pipeline targets.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Partnerships & Alliances</strong></p> <ul> <li>Identify and cultivate strategic partnerships with law firms, HR/staffing firms, real estate partners, accounting firms, and consulting networks in target markets.</li> <li>Represent the company at relevant industry events, GCC summits, and trade conferences across the US, UK, and Germany.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Marketing & Brand Building</strong></p> <ul> <li>Collaborate with leadership to develop thought leadership content, case studies, and market-specific collateral.</li> <li>Run targeted LinkedIn, email, and event-driven campaigns to generate qualified leads.</li> <li>Build the company's brand awareness among CFOs, COOs, and technology leaders in target markets.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Market Intelligence</strong></p> <ul> <li>Continuously monitor trends in GCC adoption, offshoring regulations, and competitor activity across target geographies.</li> <li>Provide actionable insights to leadership on market opportunities, pricing benchmarks, and competitive positioning.</li> </ul> <p><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></p> <p><strong>Must-Have Requirements</strong></p> <ul> <li>8 12 years of experience in B2B sales, business development, or GTM roles preferably in consulting, professional services, staffing, or technology solutions.</li> <li>Proven track record of selling to or developing relationships with buyers in the US and/or UK markets; Germany experience is a strong plus.</li> <li>Strong understanding of the GCC, offshoring, or shared services ecosystem is highly desirable.</li> <li>Demonstrated experience closing deals independently from lead generation to contract signing.</li> <li>Excellent communication, presentation, and negotiation skills, with the ability to engage C-level executives.</li> <li>Willingness to work flexible hours to align with US, UK, and Germany time zones.</li> </ul> <p><strong>Good to Have</strong></p> <ul> <li>Existing network or relationships within the GCC/offshoring ecosystem or in rel