ipient of the Sustainable Market Initiative’s Terra Carta Seal. The COP28 UAE Presidency presented ReNew the ‘Energy Transition Changemaker’ award for developing and deploying the country’s first round-the-clock power project. ReNew’s solar and wind energy projects currently contribute to 1.9% of India’s power capacity and are spread across 150+ sites and 18 Indian states. We have helped prevent 0.5% of India’s total carbon emissions and 1.1% of India’s total power sector emissions, in addition to generating around 130,000 jobs over the past decade. Job Description Roles and Responsibilities: CFO & Leadership Support: Act as an execution support partner on key initiatives, reviews, and projects. Prepare briefing notes, presentations, and executive summaries. Coordinate leadership meetings, follow up on action items, and track deliverables. Liaise with internal stakeholders, consultants, and advisors. Act as a trusted interface between the CFO office and other departments. Financial Analysis: Assist in scenario modelling, sensitivity analysis, and decisionsupport analytics. Analyze performance across business units, identify key trends, variances, and drivers, and provide actionable insights. Coordinate with business, finance, and accounting teams to resolve data gaps and clarifications. Prepare dashboards, MIS reports, and presentations as required. Business Performance & Insights: Partner with business and functional leaders to provide financial insights and recommendations. Monitor KPIs, margins, cost structures, and working capital metrics. Process Improvement & Projects Drive and support finance transformation, automation, standardization, and continuous improvement of finance processes (including CFO Office) Coordinate crossfunctional projects Support cost optimization and profitability improvement initiatives. Governance, Controls & Compliance Ensure adherence to internal financial controls, policies, and governance standards. Assist in compliance with accounting standards (Ind AS / IFRS / GAAP, as applicable). Profile & Criteria & Eligibility CA / CMA / MBA (Finance) or equivalent qualification 3+years of relevant experience in FP&A, corporate finance, consulting, CEO Office or CFO office roles Prior experience working with senior leadership is strongly preferred Role: Chief Financial Officer (CFO),Industry Type: Power,Department: Finance & Accounting,Employment Type: Full Time, PermanentRole Category: FinanceEducationPG: MBA/PGDM in Any Specialization, CA in Any Specializationread moreKey SkillsFinance ProcessFinancial AnalysisTransformationComplianceAccountingGAAPProcess ImprovementVariance AnalysisReportingGovernanceMIS ReportingCFOIND asAccounting StandardsCorporate FinanceMISCMAConsultingTransitionWorking CapitalIFRSINDReport this jobAbout the companyRenew 4.2 1.7K employee reviewsPowerTOPB2BPrivateCorporateFollow147.7k followers OverviewReNew is a leading decarbonisation solutions provider, accelerating the global transition to clean energy.Founded in 2011, ReNew has built a green energy portfolio of about 18.5 GW as of November 2, 2025—one of the largest globally. The company operates 150+ sites spread across 10 states in India. It provides decarbonisation solutions through a mix of green hydrogen, intelligent (data-driven) solutions, energy storage, manufacturing, and carbon markets.ReNew’s projects have helped generate more than 130,000 jobs, both directly and indirectly. The company has twice been recognised as a Global Lighthouse by the World Economic Forum for advancing Fourth Industrial Revolution technologies at scale and achieving impact on the ground. read moreEmbracing Diversity, Fostering InclusionWelcoming People from Diverse Backgrounds | Sumant SinhaAt ReNew, we value individual uniqueness and are dedicated to advancing progress, achieving equitable outcomes, and fostering a culture that is inclusive transcending differences of age, gender, religion, caste, etc.Company InfoLink:Renew websiteAddress: